Package sequence_generator_pkg
---------------------------------------
Description: The node inside this package generates sequences of twists setpoints based on the CoG of the bright object in the camera frame
and the relbot simulator and publishes them.
Inputs: 
/CoG
    Type: geometry_msgs/msg/Point
/output/camera_position
    Type: geometry_msgs/msg/PointStamped

Outputs:
/input/twist
    Type: geometry_msgs/msg/Twist

Run:
    In a terminal, run the following command in the cam2image_host2vm directory:
    python videoserver.py
    In a ubuntu terminal, run the following command in webcam_ws:
    ros2 launch sequence_generator_pkg sequence_generator_launch.xml

Parameters:
    depth_ : sets the queue size of the publisher/subscriber, Default = 10
    twist_strength_ : sets the twist strength in m/s or rad/s depending on linear or angular, Default =1.0
    assignment_selecter_ : sets the assignment 1.2.1(false) or 1.2.2(true), Default = true
    dt_ : sets the time interval for the sequence generation, Default = 1.0
    scaling_factor_theta_ : scales difference in x- pixel coordinates to angular velocity, Default = 0.01
    scaling_factor_x_ : scales difference in y- pixel coordinates to linear velocity, Default = 0.3

Core components:
    sequenceController() : determines difference between CoG and subimage pixel coordinates and determines and publishes twist setpoints
    publisherCallback() : publishes a 20 seconds sequence of positive and negative linear x and angular z direction twists.